    "judge_text": "**Criterion 1 \u2014 Indicator compliance:**\nAll required indicators are present: `SMA(13)`, `SMA(40)`, `RSI(14)`, and `MACD` with default settings are all instantiated correctly. MACD is created but unused in signal logic, which is a minor gap, but the three core indicators driving decisions (SMA cross, RSI) are correctly parameterized.\n\n**Criterion 2 \u2014 Problem solving:**\nThe code implements the main idea faithfully. It simulates 30-minute aggregation by sampling every `agg_bars=6` 5-minute bars, counts bullish crossovers (`crossover[-i] > 0`) over that window for `ma_crosses`, computes `avg_rsi` as the average RSI across those same 6 bars, and enters long only when `ma_crosses == 1` and `avg_rsi > 70` \u2014 exactly the assignment's entry filter. Exit logic uses `hold_bars=36` (6 periods \u00d7 6 bars = 3 hours), stop-loss at 1.5%, and take-profit at 3.0%, all matching the spec.\n\n**Criterion 3 \u2014 Relevance:**\nThe code is directly and specifically implementing this assignment's described strategy \u2014 distribution-based conditional entry using MA crossover count and average RSI as filters \u2014 with no deviation into unrelated logic.\n\nRating: [[1]]"
